      "writtenOn": "2025-12-17T10:27:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah that is fine, but I feel in a very specific case this would run into some issues:\n\nFor instance let us say I want to verify `MyVeryCoolPdf.pdf` renders fine on skia, I expect the checksum `0123456789abcdef...`\n\nNow let us say there is a CL which edits this rendering (and breaks something with this test), ending in a case where it now matches the checksum of `my_very_cool_pdf_skia.png` instead of the expected `my_very_cool_pdf_skia_mac.png`.\n\nIn the old behaviour, checksums do not match and it would still fail (as expected).\nIn the new behaviour, I assume this would compare with all images until something matches, which would say all is working correctly, even if it is not.\n\nAgain, this is extremely specific snd a very specific case that would happen (although it still could happen).",
      "parentUuid": "dd8bc1ec_d61c37e5",
